WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.540
Unexpectedly, we stayed at the president's house for the night.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.660
We were working on our new game for Summer Comiket.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.980
The game's title is

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.100
Stardust Intenzione

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.980
It's a visual novel where a sad, but beautiful and splendid, drama unfolds around Aya-san,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.580
a heroine with a special power, and Baruta-san, her fated acquaintance.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.800
I should redo this line drawing.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.390
Ha-chan?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.760
Honda Tamaki, finish the rest quickly.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.650
I'm doing it.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.160
Why is the one who suggested this the first to fall asleep?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.000
Now, now.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.920
It's not very efficient to push yourself. It'll just hurt you later.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.200
I agree. We have school tomorrow, too.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.920
Our schedule is still fine, so let's call it a day.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.920
No...

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.680
When I go back, my grandmother...

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.680
If you're awake, get up.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.930
But it's already 1:00. It's probably a neighbor who came to complain about the noise.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:35.440
Sorry to bother you at night. My name is Iino. I believe my younger sister is here.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:36.760
Your sister?

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.060
Um...

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.780
Wash your face for starters.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:43.410
Nee-san!

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.460
You!

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.740
Eh? Eh? Eh?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.790
Eh-eh-eh?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.320
Didn't I tell you to be back before curfew, Minaha?

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.720
Um... Nee-san, this...

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:17.940
Iino-san?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.440
Our grandmother is angry, too. Do you have any idea what I've been through?

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.590
Anyway, get in the car already.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.360
Iino-san, just what is going on?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.880
You were here too, Honda-san? Sorry about the commotion.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.960
We have our circumstances. We'll take care of this.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.860
See you at school, then.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.040
A surprise attack?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.200
They left.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.570
It's the first time I've seen that kind of car.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:55.050
Come to think of it, I think she said she had an older sister when we met.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.920
Is that slender girl your classmate?

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:05.320
Iino Natsu-san. She sits next to me and always shares her textbook when I forget mine.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.540
Uh? But Ha-chan is a first year too...

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.250
Maybe they're twins?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.600
But leaving that aside, we have to do something about this.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.310
The black ones... they'll hunt us down...

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.260
Don't hide behind your visitors!

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.940
The next day was Saturday, and Ha-chan didn't come to our clubroom.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:38.590
Iino, you say? Perhaps it's that massive estate? I see it on my way to my part-time job.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.500
I spoke to Iino-san in class today, too.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.570
Sorry for the inconvenience my sister has caused you.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:50.320
Minaha was forbidden from taking part in club activities in high school.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.310
We're strict about those things at home, especially our grandmother.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.380
It seems she won't be allowed to take part in Summer Comiket either.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.120
After we've worked together for so long.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.650
What should I do?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:08.160
It's a family matter. We're just going to make things more complicated if we get involved.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.540
But this game was Ha-chan's idea.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.790
Fujikawa-senpai, you wrote a song on Ha-chan's request, too.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.460
Well, that's true.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:22.160
Isn't it frustrating? To have an outsider interfere with us making a game.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.380
Just a bit.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.830
You're as cold as always.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.800
I'd rather you said I'm quick to adapt.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.540
As far as our schedule is concerned, her loss is a hard blow.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.000
It was devised with two illustrators in mind, after all.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.500
I'd like to have her back if possible.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:46.250
What do you think, Honda-chan? This way you get to draw everything yourself, as you initially hoped.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.410
I can't accept this.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:00.420
The "Stardust Intenzione" game was set in motion because Ha-chan wanted to make it at any cost.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.880
Ha-chan proposed it in the first place. She's also the one who has worked the hardest.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.580
To be forcibly taken away and prevented from taking part...

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:16.380
I'm going to Ha-chan's house. I'll talk to Iino-san and ask her to let Ha-chan come back.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.900
Direct negotiations?

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.610
Good! I was waiting to hear that!

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:24.620
Well, we won't feel satisfied if we finish our game like this.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.450
Alright! Let's head over to Iino-san's house right away!

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:32.340
We may make things more complicated if a lot of us go.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:37.000
Rather, for Shii to have a conversation with someone she just met is too tall an order.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.180
I'll go with Seki-senpai and Iris-sensei, the three of us.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.170
I'm playing two roles?

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:50.050
I'm a fellow illustrator, and if Iris-sensei is there, I'm sure Ha-chan will swell with courage!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.310
Are you going to expose my identity?

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.540
Fujikawa-senpai, tell me where Ha-chan's house is.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.180
You sure are walking fast, Honda-san.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.340
It's frustrating!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:11.080
Ha-chan's always finding fault with my drawings, and she's so self-centered.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.080
To have it end here all of a sudden!

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:19.080
You said to come as Iris-sensei, but I'm not carrying makeup today, so I can't disguise as her.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:25.220
It'll be fine! I'm sure Ha-chan will realize Seki-senpai is Iris-sensei if we tell her.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:30.040
So this glasses girl was Sensei, what a letdown.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.680
To think that I worked so hard to adapt her scenario into a game.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.360
Isn't that bad?

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.780
It's massive! Is this all the Iinos'?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.500
It's huge!

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.800
Don't you live in a big estate too?

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.200
I don't think ours is even a fifth of this.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:08:00.490
But aren't you quite wealthy? I bet you have a maid and whatnot.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:04.160
We just have one helper.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:05.840
They really have one...

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:09.560
The young mistress awaits you. Please come this way.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:10.920
Th-thank you.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.010
I am much obliged.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:16.730
The inside is huge, too.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.360
I-I see that.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:26.140
Honda-san and... a senpai from her club? So you came out of concern for Minaha? Thanks.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:30.900
Young mistress' schoolmates, I shall contact your homes if you will.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.890
Please write your contact information here.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.600
I am Seki Ayame.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.360
You may retire, Tayama-san.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.680
We're an old household, so we're quite picky about these things.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.160
I see.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.760
I wanted Minaha, at least, to live carefreely, though.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.800
Minaha, sit down.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.040
So far, whenever our relatives were angry at Minaha because of the curfew or her grades,

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:01.960
I appeased them, within my limits.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.100
Always emphasizing our house's rules and customs... they're quite old-fashioned.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:12.160
But these past few weeks she's been coming home even later than usual,

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:17.580
she always goes out on her days off, she stays up late, and her grades are dropping.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.260
I've been unable to make up for it.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:26.020
It was particularly bad yesterday. Our grandmother was boiling with rage.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.500
Minaha, don't you have something to say to Honda-san and your senpai?

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.260
I'm sorry.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.200
Look at people when you're apologizing!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.720
Good grief...

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:41.350
It's not like drawing and club activities are worth being so persistent. Right, Honda-san?

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.360
You say that some people do it for a living,

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.480
but it's not like you're aiming to become a professional yourself.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.360
Nee-san, I've always liked-

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.460
I'm tired of hearing that, Minaha.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:54.820
How you're adapting this story you've always been passionate about into a game and all that.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.560
Do you need to become invested in that right now?

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:00.810
There are plenty of people who draw as a hobby.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.700
Are you saying that it doesn't make a difference who draws?

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.900
I can draw things that no one else can-

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:10.840
That's conceit. Anyone can make something that no one else can.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:12.700
Honda-san, for example.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.290
She's being talked into it.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:20.060
She's glaring at me! I'm sure she's going to take it out on me.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:26.520
Do you understand? The world won't end because you didn't draw this.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:30.900
You need to be more aware of your role as the youngest Iino daughter.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:38.390
There are plenty of people who draw as a hobby. There are also plenty of people better than me.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:42.120
It is conceited to think there's something only I can do.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.740
But if I don't draw, who will?

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.100
That's wrong.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:50.920
You're wrong about that, Onee-san.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:52.580
How so?

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:59.560
Hoping to change something, or to be useful to someone, is not the reason why you create things.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.040
You make them because you enjoy it, because you're alive.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:05.690
Just like eating and breathing.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:10.040
Your hands are giving birth to a new story.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.720
There is no value and no meaning.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.400
It's because of the act of creating that you can take pride in your life.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.120
Wh-what's a homely glasses girl doing looking so cool?

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.360
Eh, what? She's turning tsundere from this?

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.660
Eh, you take pride in your life from the act of creating...

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:29.680
Then the poems you wrote for your grade school anthology are the foundation of your life.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.080
Isn't that right?

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:35.820
As expected of Iino-san, she's used to dealing with this type of person.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:40.020
Th-that's right! All my works are related to who I am now.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.440
Then, Tayama-san.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:47.900
Seki Ayame-san, here is Sukimoto Elementary School's 78th anthology.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:51.600
Please read us that work you take such pride in.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.650
Don't hold back.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.480
What's with this coordination?

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:59.400
"The voice of the you that I'll meet someday...

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.520
seemed to be floating by my window.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.720
What if time was blown inside until it rusted,

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:08.600
I think, as I keep ever searching for tomorrow's retrospective.

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:12.720
I look up at the night sky, that seems to wither, as I sing, I sing.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.820
A voice so white that it has no echo.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.720
I see nothing, nothing.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.640
I hear nothing, reach nothing.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.080
In a town distorted by nihilism.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.180
The insensible sign that reverberates."

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.020
No way... What is this feeling welling up in my chest?

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:31.820
My heart is throbbing at the glasses girl's poem!

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.940
I can't! I have Iris-sensei.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.330
Ha-chan really likes the things Seki-senpai writes.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.260
That was embarrassing...

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.160
It's okay.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:48.140
In deference to senpai, I'll try to persuade our grandmother once again.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.750
But there is one condition

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:55.680
Minaha and Honda-san, both of you must get at least 70 points in every subject in the finals.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.710
All of them?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.040
Me too?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:02.040
You did quite poorly on the last test too.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:05.700
You must prove that you can do your club and your studies.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:11.880
Or rather, that by studying together with your clubmates, you can improve your grades.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.360
That will make it easy for me to persuade our grandmother.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.320
Our guest room can host an overnighter.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.690
Help yourselves to our fridge, too.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.040
Déjà vu!

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.240
Then let's start with chemistry, which covers the most material.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:30.040
Endou-sensei is strict, so memorize those chemical formulas thoroughly!

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:30.860
Eh?

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:34.480
Ehhhh?

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.920
The tests are over.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.240
Good work.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:47.760
I won't get a perfect score, but I think I can get 90 points.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:50.430
I studied so hard at Iino-san's house, too.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:54.860
But it was so difficult, particularly the last questions.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.850
The last ones? They were nearly the same as in the textbook.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.740
No, I mean questions five and six after that.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:02.600
Huh?

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.450
There were more questions in the back side!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.640
How are you doing, Honda Tamaki?

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.510
Sorry, Ha-chan, I fell asleep for a bit.

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.000
Are you all right? Make sure you don't catch a cold.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.600
I was dreaming about the last day of tests.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:26.020
I missed the questions on the back side and lost a lot of points.

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:26.470
Hey...

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:30.700
that was what I did, you got a high grade.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:35.430
I just barely got 70 points and have to study more because of that.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.100
Do your homework properly.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:43.120
I'll go back to work. I'm not done with that sprite I wanted to finish up two days ago.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:46.490
I'll get to work as soon as I finish studying, too. See you later.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.040
It gets tough when the deadline approaches...

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.450
There's less than two weeks left.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:57.410
Papa... I'm sad knowing you'll be working away from home this week too,

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.800
but you have to work hard at your job, right?

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.810
Ah, I'm low on Papa energy!

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:06.950
What do you usually do to your father? That's some cutesy voice.

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:09.780
Ah, I didn't hang up!

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:15.360
It seems I've always been drawing these past few days.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:20.680
Come to think of it, this time last year I used to play card games in the living room a lot.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.960
This was fun... I got so excited when I played with Yumine too.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.490
Hello, Ha-chan? I was working properly.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:44.060
I got sidetracked from studying and was absorbed in Iris-sensei's works for about an hour.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.300
Sorry, I was reading an unrelated book too.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.130
Let's both do our best.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:56.080
I was drawing this picture earlier. The coloring's not very good, I'd like to do it over...

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:58.080
Oi! You can't do that!

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:02.220
You feel like redoing your drawings sometimes too, Ha-chan!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:06.040
I always do! But we have to push forward!

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.780
I'm happy you understand!

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:14.420
With this workmanship, Ha-chan may make fun of me if I show this to her.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.450
These past few days I've always been coloring.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:21.520
I wonder why?

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:27.950
Are you saying that it doesn't make a difference who draws? I can draw things that no one else can-

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.800
That's conceit.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:35.240
I see. I suppose it doesn't matter if I'm the one drawing this.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:53.740
I shouldn't be thinking these things... I'm feeling a litte gloomy.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:55.880
There is no value and no meaning.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.870
It's because of the act of creating that you can take pride in your life.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:03.120
Even though Seki-senpai said that...

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:10.200
I have to go back and keep working. My drawings are being mixed with Ha-chan's, right?

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:16.520
I guess she'll say that my drawings don't suit Seki-senpai's scenario and such again.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.520
I wonder why I draw?

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:23.680
Good evening.

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:24.340
Ah?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:28.940
If you'd like, how about we talk?

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.160
I feel somewhat half-hearted.

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:39.800
Isn't it weird? After I told Ha-chan that we had to finish it for Summer Comiket,

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.900
and that I'd draw lots of pictures...

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:47.020
Originally, it was Ha-chan who invited me to draw with her,

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.080
and I thought I didn't need to try very hard.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:54.660
That's no good, right? Can you scold me, Teru-san?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:06.780
If you can't get in the mood, that must be your heart telling you it's not enjoying it.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:11.160
The things that you want to draw, and that you want to do... this isn't it, right?

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:13.700
Hey, what do you want to do?

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.640
I want to be pampered.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.260
I want to be pampered by Papa.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:20.760
Eh?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.660
Why can't you be Papa, Teru-san?

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.220
I wonder why...

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.450
How much do you love your dad, Tamatama-chan?

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.040
I love him a lot!

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:37.130
I've always liked reading the manga featuring old men that Papa had in his library.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:42.900
I used to try tracing them a lot, but Papa was cooler than any manga character.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:49.000
While I drew, I used to think that I'd like to draw an old man as cool as my papa.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.310
Ah, did I say something embarrassing?

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:56.270
That's it. See, you found it. The reason why you draw.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:58.450
You just have to express that feeling.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:02.920
Thank you very much!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.680
I feel like my heart is lighter. I think I can draw.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:11.860
Cool men. Cool men like Papa.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:15.380
Papa?

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:17.730
Ah, it's Ha-chan.

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:21.800
Wait a moment! That's your reaction to finding me here?

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:26.710
It was a pain to come all the way here. It's the train's last stop.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:28.840
Ah, thanks for coming.

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:30.270
You're doing that on purpose!

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:35.500
Sorry about earlier. I may have pressured you to work.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.880
Not at all.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.360
I haven't thanked you for earlier, either.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:40.540
Earlier?

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:48.320
Th-thanks. You help me with my tests, and with making games. I'm glad.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:53.290
I'm glad that I could study so hard too. That was thanks to you.

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:54.840
Honda Tamaki...

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:59.760
So I'll do my best with drawing. Drawing old men!

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.220
Old men?

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:04.500
Grandma, I'm home.

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:08.490
I'm not satisfied, so I'll draw some old men as a supplement.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:09.740
A-at this stage?

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:12.330
Why did you come to my house, too?

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:16.770
You're slow to react. I'll work here for two or three hours before going back.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.760
I came here with that purpose.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:19.900
Eh? Really?

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:23.360
I think we'll progress faster if we work together.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:24.980
We can watch each other.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:28.910
No, I mean, if you stay three hours you won't have a train back.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:30.340
Today's a holiday.

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:33.880
It's true! Just how far in the middle of nowhere do you live?

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.480
It ain't nowhere! Actually, it might be.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:41.030
Wh-what about the curfew? I'll be scolded again if I stay over for the night again.

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:43.550
I think you'll be fine if you go back now.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.510
Then what was the point of coming?

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:53.800
I guess I'll send a message... but maybe Nee-san can cover for me somehow...

00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:58.800
There's no need to worry!

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:03.330
Because I'm determined to not go home today either!

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.320
Why are you coming in through the window?

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:06.700
That's what you react to?

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:11.900
Ah, thinking won't solve anything! This is a revelation from Lady Iris!

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.410
She went from a writer to a god.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.600
A revelation that says to work in earnest here today.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:19.630
We're making it to summer Comiket without problems, Honda Tamaki!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:20.460
Mm!

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.220
Ah, in this situation...

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:29.140
This time it should be me who says "leave drinks to me" while opening the fridge, right?

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:32.500
But I haven't prepared that much. Sorry.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.120
There's no need for that.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:36.620
All right, there's less than two weeks before the deadline!

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:37.870
Let's do it!

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:43.140
In the end, both Ha-chan and Teru-senpai stayed for the night.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.540
Summer Comiket is in three weeks.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:25.980
I forgot something very important!

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:28.100
The reason I originally joined this club.

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:32.990
It wasn't just to draw pictures, but to make a game that would make someone smile!
